  <diagram name="Scope and Findings" id="w05-findings">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1561" dy="798" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#183c43;align=left;" value="Week 5 | Scope and Findings" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="1070" x="45" y="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="scope" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;1 · Process scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Jose Romero. The purpose of the appointment process is to illustrate how it actually functions and where the handoff becomes unclear. It begins with a visitor that requests for an appointment, it ends with the visitor being passed over to the next staff team in the instance that the readiness status checks out properly. What falls outside of the diagram is the assessment of why in fact the readiness decision is missing." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="1070" x="45" y="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="walkthrough" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · Check the two paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;The gap is supported by W05-S04 because&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;no completed readiness decision was present in the supplied trace before arrival. At intake, held slots will enter exception review. However, the trace is unable to prove an action never happened.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="215" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · Evidence and model review&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;Source W05-S01 is able to record the request slot along with the support preferences. The held slot recorded is supported by W05-S02, because if there is unavailability a held status is retained. Then, in W05-S03, with the visitor arriving, the appointment is located and readiness is checked. Here the ready appointment will proceed to support arrangement confirmation to the next staff team. Furthermore, in W05-S03, the held appointments will enter exception review with scheduling and clinical operations. I made corrections to how the held status is determined.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff));&quot;&gt;The remaining uncertainty is that no completed readiness decision is present in the supplied trace before arrival, and it does not tell why that decision is unavailable. The record needed to resolve it is source W05-S02 since a held status is retained and capacity is reviewed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="reflection" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" value="&lt;b&gt;4 · Learning reflection (reuse your Discord paragraph)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;The current model process became clearer because it illustrated the very start, from the visitor requesting the appointment, all the way to the end of a successful appointment reaching the next staff team. Additionally, following the appointment from request to intake cleared up which departments handle what specifically, and how the incident became uncertain. Responsibility is unclear for determining why the trace in W05-S04 failed to show a completed readiness decision arriving at intake. Process modeling differs from the Week 4 requirements because the modeling illustrates the process from initialization to the end, while the requirements were intended to demonstrate what is necessary.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="1070" x="45" y="525" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="evidence" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=14;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" value="&lt;b&gt;5 · Portfolio evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;[Editable model filename and Week05/Evidence/Week05_Discord_Post.png or .jpg. If Discord is unavailable, identify the equivalent reflection used here.]&lt;br&gt;Save the .drawio file; export both pages as one PDF; check readability; commit and push." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="1070" x="45" y="680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
